<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:16:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo arrives in Uruguay for first stop on 12-day South America tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-pope-leo-arrives-in-uruguay-for-first-stop-on-12-day-south-america-tour</link><description>
Pope Leo touched down in Uruguay on Friday to begin a 12-day tour of South America that will also see him visit Argentina and Peru. The tour is seen as something of a homecoming for the pontiff who lived in Peru for almost two decades and holds joint US and Peruvian citizenship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3283e0f4-da24-11f1-a6d8-95d5f1845f91</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:14:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump announces immigration hardliner Stephen Miller as new chief of staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-announces-immigration-hardliner-stephen-miller-as-new-chief-of-staff</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday said advisor Stephen Miller would become his new chief of staff. Miller has been instrumental in driving the Trump administration's mass deportation programme and faced particular criticism after the deadly shootings of two Minneapolis protesters by ICE agents in January.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac163ece-da21-11f1-a81a-0383cf3d852d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:51:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg">© Chip Somodevilla, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Midterms: A Maga PostMortem, Europe’s ‘Shape Shifting’ Protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261106-midterms-a-maga-postmortem-europe-s-shape-shifting-protests</link><description>
A World This Week ‘Mid Terms Special’ 
 
Gavin Lee is joined by panel of four distinguished international correspondents to assess the aftermath of the worst Republican election result since the 1970s, post Watergate. We ask, is peak MAGA over? What will now change at home and abroad? And who ends the week in pole position as Presidential frontrunner for 2028?
 
We also consider the scale and scope of Europe Wide Protests:  
 
This week housing organisations, trade unions and activist groups from seven countries met in Paris issuing a joint call for demonstrations. Are the national protest movements becoming a coordinated European movement?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7761de0-da1d-11f1-8391-1b8f54bdb46f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:08:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>A homegrown Georgia moderate and pragmatist: Is Senator Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-a-homegrown-georgia-moderate-and-pragmatist-is-senator-ossoff-the-future-of-the-democratic-party</link><description>
Is Senator Jon Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party? Following a resounding midterm victory in Georgia, a former Republican stronghold, the 39-year-old senator has emerged as a prominent figure as the Democrats look ahead to 2028 for their next presidential nominee. His natural confidence, polished media performances and ability to appeal to a diverse electorate have prompted comparisons with Barack Obama. Yet behind the excitement surrounding his national prospects lies a more complicated question: whether political momentum in the Senate necessarily translates into a presidential frontrunner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bf03f84-da1b-11f1-b582-41f7c3676cec</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 19:49:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What Trump’s midterms debacle could mean for US support for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-what-trump-s-midterms-debacle-could-mean-for-us-support-for-ukraine</link><description>
The Republican Party's crushing defeat in midterm elections has left Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky optimistic about future support for Kyiv and stronger transatlantic relations. But with US President Donald Trump retaining broad foreign policy powers, the Democratic majority in Congress may have limited scope to bring about substantial change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da1effc4-d9de-11f1-837c-91cdb8d44ed0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:49:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg">© Kylie Cooper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US midterms mark 'the beginning of the end' for Trump, John Bolton says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261106-us-midterms-mark-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump-john-bolton-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, John Bolton, who served as national security adviser to Donald Trump during his first term, called the US midterm results "the beginning of the end" for Trump's stranglehold on the Republican Party. Democrats regained control of both the House of Representatives and the Senate earlier this week, marking the Republicans' worst performance since the 1974 elections in the wake of the Watergate scandal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3e0d66-d9f8-11f1-8676-4f5175760546</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 17:26:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe: What we know about the hoax bomb threats disrupting flights</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-what-we-know-about-the-hoax-bomb-threats-disrupting-flights</link><description>
Dozens of European flights have been disrupted this week after bomb threats were sent in to various airports, with fighter planes escorting many civilian aircraft after threats were called in mid-flight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/821a507a-da02-11f1-960f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/821a507a-da02-11f1-960f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97255028-da02-11f1-bb76-5534a78b8157</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:59:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-and-three-sexual-assaults</link><description>
British comedian Russell Brand was on Thursday, November 5, found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults by a London jury, including a 16-year-old girl. He now faces "significant" prison time, according to the judge. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/090853f4-da01-11f1-95a1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b57246d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/090853f4-da01-11f1-95a1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b57246d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1dad8d2-da00-11f1-ad93-c33636d1bed4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:45:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pressure mounts on US Defence chief Hegseth after Republican election rout</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pressure-mounts-on-us-defence-chief-hegseth-after-republican-election-rout</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth is under growing pressure, with victorious Democrats planning to target him in Congress and Republicans blaming the Iran war he championed for their election losses. President Donald Trump has stood by Hegseth so far, insisting he's doing "a very good job".  But Trump and Vice President JD Vance have both blamed midterm election losses on the Iran war, for which Hegseth is a key advocate and spokesman.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6399eb0-d9ff-11f1-8b14-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-170741-170927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6399eb0-d9ff-11f1-8b14-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-170741-170927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb4263f6-d9ff-11f1-b89a-57ffd87dc22e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:45:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'Trump is a very dangerous person for the world': EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-trump-is-a-very-dangerous-person-for-the-world-eu-s-former-top-diplomat-josep-borrell</link><description>
In an interview with Talking Europe, the EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell reacts to the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections, warning that US President Donald Trump is still "a very dangerous person for the world".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1462964-d9f1-11f1-8b86-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-JOSEP-BORRELL-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1462964-d9f1-11f1-8b86-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-JOSEP-BORRELL-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b329fcd4-d6af-11f1-af0c-4789fb9a1a2f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:44:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Chaos within aviation industry' as European air traffic hit by bomb threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-chaos-within-aviation-industry-as-european-air-traffic-hit-by-bomb-threats</link><description>
Officials across Europe reported a fresh slew of bomb threats against multiple flights on Friday, November 6, following a string of hoaxes that have caused flight diversions this week. Two broadcasters also received security threats, in a possible sign the menace was spreading beyond the skies. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1649d436-d9ff-11f1-b43d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5cd1fe0d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1649d436-d9ff-11f1-b43d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5cd1fe0d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96eb94c8-d9fd-11f1-8429-d76a332baec9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:33:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wounded French protesters to sue interior minister over police brutality</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261106-wounded-french-protesters-to-sue-interior-minister-over-police-brutality</link><description>
Around ten demonstrators wounded at recent protests in France on Friday said they will sue Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez over police brutality. Student and cost-of-living protests in recent weeks have been marred by violence, including reports of police inflicting serious and lifechanging injuries on protesters – many of whom are minors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1048d660-d9fd-11f1-b727-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/a4006db62a56c37deb8c8a26aeee10ea06d43a11.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1048d660-d9fd-11f1-b727-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/a4006db62a56c37deb8c8a26aeee10ea06d43a11.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">119d92ee-d9fd-11f1-9d63-93464729b409</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:13:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1048d660-d9fd-11f1-b727-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/a4006db62a56c37deb8c8a26aeee10ea06d43a11.jpg">© Simon Wohlfahrt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Turkey to push for 'electrification' drive at COP31 as climate threats mount</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261106-turkey-to-push-for-electrification-drive-at-cop31-as-climate-threats-mount</link><description>
COP31 host Turkey is set to push for a "electrification" drive to help meet global elergy demand as the UN climate conference kicks off in Antalya on Monday. The annual summit takes place this year under the shadow of a cost-of-living crisis fuelled by the war in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79a8343e-d9f3-11f1-ba9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6HQ8CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79a8343e-d9f3-11f1-ba9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6HQ8CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a802726c-d9f4-11f1-a30c-21a184e14c21</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:36:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79a8343e-d9f3-11f1-ba9d-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6HQ8CQ.jpg">© Goksel Yapar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>China keeps a close eye on US midterm shake-up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261106-china-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-shake-up</link><description>
The US midterm elections have resulted in the Democratic Party taking control of both chambers of the US Congress, leaving Donald Trump as a lame duck president for the remainder of his term. Professor Steve Tsang of the SOAS China Institute tells FRANCE 24 that, while a weakened Trump could strengthen Beijing's negotiating position, the Chinese leadership is aware that Congress has relatively little sway over foreign policy and is keen to maintain warm personal ties between the two presidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12d8854c-d9da-11f1-a55a-c728c64c10de</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:03:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo embarks on Latin America trip with a first stop in Uruguay</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pope-leo-embarks-on-latin-america-trip-with-a-first-stop-in-uruguay</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV is kicking off a three-nation tour of Latin America on Friday, November 6, with a visit to Uruguay, the region’s least Catholic and most secular country, three weeks after undergoing lung cancer surgery that had put the entire trip into question. After Uruguay, he will then go to Argentina and Peru. FRANCE 24's Hanna Roberts has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5bee38e6-d9ec-11f1-b58a-d3ec7f982f66</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:58:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>California governor to grant clemency to all 548 death row inmates in state</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-to-grant-clemency-to-all-548-death-row-inmates-in-state</link><description>
California's governor Gavy Newsom announced Thursday that he will commute all death sentences in the state to life without the possibility of parole. He said that "capital punishment is morally wrong." The state Supreme Court will have the final say in hundreds of those cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7555a644-d9eb-11f1-b34b-9de4add3b6a8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:54:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>The women who rode the blue wave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261106-the-women-who-rode-the-blue-wave</link><description>
In this edition, we report on how the US midterms, which saw the Democrats make massive gains, also marked a series of historic firsts for women. Also the dark side to Bangkok's booming fertility industry, which attracts thousands of foreign patients seeking assistance from the Thai capital's state-of-the-art private clinics. Plus how an impoverished neighbourhood in El Salvador, once a no-go zone plagued by gang violence, is being transformed by women into a vibrant canvas for street art.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cd75936-d922-11f1-86b5-ef0b033d2e60</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:15:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Too early to draw conclusions' as bomb threat hoaxes target European countries</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-too-early-to-draw-conclusions-as-bomb-threat-hoaxes-target-european-countries</link><description>
Several Irish media outlets reported receiving bomb threats on Friday as a wave of hoax alerts that had so far mainly targeted airlines continued across Europe, with more than a dozen new flights affected. No explosives have been found in any of the incidents so far. European authorities are scrambling to identify the sources of the threats, as FRANCE 24's Brussels correspondent Dave Keating reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edce07d8-d9e6-11f1-aa0f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-140157-140614-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edce07d8-d9e6-11f1-aa0f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-140157-140614-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f304c084-d9e6-11f1-af35-736eb6218a73</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:48:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paraguay's Peña offers resignation amid banking scandal, protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-paraguay-s-pe%C3%B1a-offers-resignation-amid-banking-scandal-protests</link><description>
Paraguayan President Santiago Peña submitted his resignation on Thursday, but Congress put it on hold as impeachment proceedings against him move forward. Peña is facing impeachment over a banking scandal that has affected millions of people and sparked protests, with thousands taking to the streets in recent days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41af145a-d9e7-11f1-9a4d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-141452-141644-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41af145a-d9e7-11f1-9a4d-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-141452-141644-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46934fa4-d9e7-11f1-9b5f-43e46b44a010</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:45:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump’s stillborn diesel deal: Why Russian oil tankers are not heading to the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-stillborn-diesel-deal-why-russian-oil-tankers-are-not-heading-to-the-us</link><description>
The first oil tankers scheduled to deliver Russian diesel to the US under a deal between President Donald Trump and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin have changed course and are no longer heading toward the US coast. It spells the end of an agreement announced with great fanfare before the midterms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72572b5c-d9d7-11f1-aa8a-15a9cc0740e7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:38:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png">© Studio graphique France Médias Monde</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Is Israel opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot going to replace Benjamin Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu</link><description>
In Israel, Gadi Eisenkot emerged on Thursday, November 5, as the frontrunner to be tasked with forming a government. This comes after one of the two main parties representing ultra-Orthodox Jewish voters – a longtime ally of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition – declined to recommend any candidate for the task. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebb71fde-d9cd-11f1-a086-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-04af7880.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebb71fde-d9cd-11f1-a086-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-04af7880.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8163f792-d9cd-11f1-b042-e7fb1d136a6b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:25:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future in question after midterms setback</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-defence-secretary-pete-hegseth-s-future-in-question-after-midterms-setback</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future is in question after Tuesday's, November 3, midterms setback. On Thursday, November 5, he issued a video message vowing to fight efforts in Congress to impeach him and defending the ‌Iran war as “courageous and historic”. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee8dbbc0-d9d5-11f1-bdf5-e56d28bb9ded</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tech giants lose $1 trillion in one day after Democrats victory in midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-tech-giants-lose-1-trillion-in-one-day-after-democrats-victory-in-midterms</link><description>
Trillions of dollars have been wiped off the stock value of major tech firms in the US, Europe and Asia. Investors appear worried about the possibility of an AI slowdown and tougher regulation as Democrats won the midterms in the US. Some of the Democratic candidates had expressed their opposition to the data centres that are needed to power AI technology.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d57022c-d9dc-11f1-817e-cfc74dac3b1b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canada PM Mark Carney unveils budget to strengthen economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-canada-pm-mark-carney-unveils-budget-to-strengthen-economy</link><description>
Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled his first ever budget on November 5, which set out strong ambitions for greater economic independence from the US. The "Masters of our Destiny" budget also announced generous measures for parts of the economy affected by tariffs, setting aside 44 billion Canadian dollars for impacted businesses and workers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56f49bae-d9de-11f1-9e2c-cd4b49fae717</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:10:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
